      <div style="max-width: 850px;">
        <h3 style="color: var(--white); margin-bottom: 1rem;">What is Beckham Law?</h3>
        <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82);">The Beckham Law is a special tax regime that allows newly arrived expat residents to pay a flat 24% tax rate on Spanish-source income (up to €600,000 annually) instead of Spain's progressive tax brackets, which go up to 47%. This applies to employees, self-employed individuals, and business owners.</p>

        <h3 style="color: var(--white); margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Eligibility Requirements</h3>
        <ul style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82);">
          <li>You must not have been a Spanish tax resident in the previous 10 years</li>
          <li>You must relocate to Spain and become a tax resident</li>
          <li>The regime applies for 4 consecutive tax years</li>
          <li>You must apply within 3 months of becoming a Spanish resident</li>
          <li>Only Spanish-source income qualifies (not foreign income)</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="color: var(--white); margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Estimated Tax Savings</h3>
        <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82); margin-bottom: 1rem;">For a DNV applicant earning €50,000 annually:</p>
        <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding: 1.2rem; border-radius: 8px; border-left: 3px solid var(--yellow);">
          <p style="color: var(--yellow); margin: 0;"><strong>Regular Tax:</strong> ~€17,500–€19,000 (after deductions)</p>
          <p style="color: var(--yellow); margin: 0.8rem 0 0;">><strong>Beckham Law:</strong> €12,000 (24% flat rate)</p>
          <p style="color: var(--yellow); margin: 0.8rem 0 0;"><strong>Annual Savings:</strong> €5,000–€7,000</p>
        </div>

        <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82); margin-top: 1.5rem;">Higher earners see even greater savings. Use our tax calculator to compare your personal tax liability under both regimes.</p>
